Please put the quote in context. It is that kind of omission that
angers me the most by what David says and turns his hostile messages
into cheap shots.

Let me ask this question of you
  Why do YOU want to come back more than once from Gehennom?

I consider repeatedly entering / exiting Gehennom to consolidate loot
to be a waste of time. By that point of the game you should have more
than enough of every item needed to ascend. The speed ascenders like
Rast seem to prove that over and over again.

Let me give you an example. I just ascended a Tourist in the Devnull
Tournament. I had teleport control, but only two cursed teleport
scrolls and limited uncursed ones. I took a nominal amount of stuff in
the BoH and did a controlled teleport to level 99 (sorry...) and did
the bottom up method to map the levels. I picked up selected loot
(primarily full healing potions) but didn't find much to help the
ascension otherwise. Some of the stuff was dumped in convenient places
like Vlad's entry (as I left) or in the water on the Juiblex level to
prevent use by monsters. I did bless a few enchant weapon scrolls at
the sanctum to bring my dual sabers & daggers to +6 (from +5) and
sorted through the robes to improve my spell failure rates. No reason I
could see for returning to or above the castle.

Its that kind of experience - over and over again - that leads me to
recommend people to get properly prepared & go down & up. I also
mention the alternatives as well. Its this kind of balanced
recommendation that I believe should be provided at this point.

